index 184b04e63c579..ae34ef32d7831 100644
--- a/doc/source/whatsnew/v3.1.0.rst
+++ b/doc/source/whatsnew/v3.1.0.rst
@@ -1144,6 +1144,7 @@ Sparse
 - Bug in :meth:`Series.argmin`, :meth:`Series.argmax`, :meth:`Series.idxmin`, :meth:`Series.idxmax`, :meth:`DataFrame.idxmin`, :meth:`DataFrame.idxmax`, :meth:`SparseArray.argmin`, and :meth:`SparseArray.argmax` raising ``ValueError: attempt to get argmin of an empty sequence`` on :class:`SparseDtype` data with no non-missing stored values, when the non-missing ``fill_value`` occupies at least one position, instead of returning the first such position (:issue:`68462`)
 - Bug in :meth:`Series.cumsum`, :meth:`Series.cumprod`, :meth:`Series.cummin`, :meth:`Series.cummax` and their :class:`DataFrame` counterparts raising ``NotImplementedError`` on :class:`SparseDtype` data (:issue:`68187`)
 - Bug in :meth:`Series.mean` with ``skipna=False`` ignoring missing values for :class:`SparseDtype`-backed :class:`Series` (:issue:`65478`)
+- Bug in :meth:`Series.mean`, :meth:`DataFrame.mean`, and :meth:`SparseArray.mean` on :class:`SparseDtype` data with no non-missing values, an empty array included, emitting a numpy ``RuntimeWarning``, or raising ``ZeroDivisionError`` for an object subtype or ``TypeError`` for a non-numeric ``fill_value``; the missing value is now returned quietly (:issue:`68484`)
 - Bug in :meth:`Series.memory_usage`, :meth:`DataFrame.memory_usage`, and :meth:`Index.memory_usage` with ``deep=True``, :meth:`DataFrame.info` with ``memory_usage="deep"``, and ``sys.getsizeof`` raising ``TypeError`` on an object subtype :class:`SparseDtype`; :meth:`SparseArray.memory_usage` is new (:issue:`68490`)
 - Bug in :meth:`Series.mode` and :meth:`DataFrame.mode` raising ``AttributeError: 'SparseDtype' object has no attribute 'itemsize'`` on a float :class:`SparseDtype` column (:issue:`68421`)
 - Bug in :meth:`Series.reindex` and alignment raising when extending a boolean :class:`SparseDtype`-backed :class:`Series`; missing entries now upcast to ``object`` to match the dense behavior (:issue:`32119`)
